  "notes.eyebrow": "SCENE NOTES",
  "notes.index.pageTitle": "Scene Notes · 3D Gallery · Dango Travels",
  "notes.index.metaDescription": "Notes for all 26 three.js scenes: the original prompt, the code size and detected three.js techniques of every AI-model version, and the differences recorded after reading each version's source.",
  "notes.index.heading": "Scene Notes",
  "notes.index.lead": "Every one of the 26 scenes in the 3D gallery has a notes page: what it depicts, the original prompt, which techniques each model version used, and what becomes visible when each version's source is read alongside the others.",
  "notes.index.p1": "These pages are reading notes, not marketing copy. The file sizes, line counts and technique tags in each version table are measured directly from 3d/<id><suffix>/index.html by tools/gen_notes.py; the comparison notes were written after reading each version's structure, animation, lighting and interaction. Every version of a scene was given the same prompt, so the differences come mainly from how each model interpreted the task and organised geometry and interaction.",
  "notes.index.p2": "To see a scene running, open “Compare all versions” from any notes page, or go back to the 3D gallery and play a collection by category. Every prompt is published under 3d/prompts/ and can be copied to reproduce the experiment.",
