  "notes.comparisonHeading": "Comparison notes",
  "notes.comparisonNote": "These observations come from reading each version's source. They describe only structural, animation and interaction differences visible in the code, without turning the experiment into a leaderboard.",
  "notes.howHeading": "How it was made",
  "notes.howP1": "The same prompt was given to each model below. It asks for a single HTML file that opens directly in a modern browser, with three.js loaded at a pinned version through a CDN import map; all geometry, materials and textures must be generated procedurally, with no external models or images.",
  "notes.howP2": "The result is published as a static page on GitHub Pages, with no build step and no backend. The sizes, line counts and technique tags on this page are measured from the generated source; the original prompts are published under 3d/prompts/ so the experiment can be checked or reproduced.",
  "notes.howP3": "Before publishing, the page is checked for loading, usable interaction and a sensible mobile layout, and small site-level integration fixes are made when needed; the scene content itself is generated by the model. The model notes for each version are listed below.",
